rarian bought 300 books.\n   - Last year, the librarian bought \\( x \\times 300 \\) books.\n   - This year, the librarian donated 200 books.\n\n2. **Calculate the number of books in the library after each year:**\n   - Five years ago: 500 books\n   - Three years ago: \\( 500 + 300 = 800 \\) books\n   - Two years ago: \\( 800 + 300 = 1100 \\) books\n   - Last year: \\( 1100 + x \\times 300 \\) books\n   - This year: \\( 1100 + x \\times 300 - 200 = 1100 + x \\times 300 - 200 = 900 + x \\times 300 \\) books\n\n3. **Determine the total number of books in the library now:**\n   - We know the total number of books in the library now is 1400.\n   - Therefore, we set up the equation: \\( 900 + x \\times 300 = 1400 \\).\n\n4. **Solve for \\( x \\):**\n   \\[\n   900 + 300x = 1400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   300x = 1400 - 900\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   300x = 500\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{500}{300}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{5}{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of the unknown variable \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}\\).\n\nGiven set A={m-3, 2m^{2}+m}, if 0 is an element of A, then the value of the real number m is (　　)\nA: -2\nB: -3\nC: -2 or-3\nD: 0\n\nTo determine the value of the real number \\( m \\) such that \\( 0 \\) is an element of set \\( A = \\{m-3, 2m^2 + m\\} \\), we need to set each element of the set equal to \\( 0 \\) and solve for \\( m \\).\n\nThe set \\( A \\) contains two elements: \\( m-3 \\) and \\( 2m^2 + m \\). Therefore, we have two possible equations:\n1. \\( m - 3 = 0 \\)\n2. \\( 2m^2 + m = 0 \\)\n\nLet's solve each equation separately.\n\n**Solving the first equation:**\n\\[ m - 3 = 0 \\]\n\\[ m = 3 \\]\n\nNow, we need to check if this value of \\( m \\) satisfies the condition that \\( 0 \\) is an element of the set \\( A \\). We substitute \\( m = 3 \\) into the elements of the set \\( A \\):\n\\[ m - 3 = 3 - 3 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 2m^2 + m = 2(3)^2 + 3 = 2 \\cdot 9 + 3 = 18 + 3 = 21 \\]\nSo, the set \\( A \\) becomes \\( \\{0, 21\\} \\), and indeed, \\( 0