      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we start by simplifying the expression \\( -3737 \\mod 8 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when 3737 is divided by 8. We perform the division:\n\n\\[ 3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\n\nThis can be written as:\n\n\\[ 3737 = 8 \\cdot 467 + 1. \\]\n\nSo, the remainder when 3737 is divided by 8 is 1. Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[ 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nSince we need the congruence to be in the form \\( n \\equiv a \\pmod{8} \\) with \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\), we convert \\(-1\\) to a positive equivalent by adding 8:\n\n\\[ -1 + 8 = 7. \\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nSo, the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies the given condition is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{7}. \\]",
